179531	179654	179528	179528	Blanche	257	“ Several years ago there was a fair young girl , none too rich , in our station of life . A gentleman , who was none too rich either , sought and gained her love . He could not marry ; he was not rich , I say . They loved on in secret , hoping for better times , she wearing out her years and her heart . Oh , Alice ! I can not describe to you how she loved him -- how she has continued to love him up to this moment . Through evil report she clung to him tenaciously and tenderly as the vine clings to its trellis , for the world spoke ill of him . ”
